            <ArticleTitle>Clinical contribution of the collateral circulation to myocardial protection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>393-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This section describes the clinical evidence for benefit from coronary collateral channels. There is data to suggest the presence of a protective effect in patients sustaining myocardial infarction regardless of whether they receive reperfusion therapy, and whether the collaterals were preformed. The role of pre-infarction angina in stimulating collateral development remains a contentious issue.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
